e': 'user', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.content': '\n        Task: Generate a precise command to execute the selected tool.\n\nContext:\n- **Query:** There is a collection of $25$ indistinguishable white chips and $25$ indistinguishable black chips. Find the number of ways to place some of these chips in the $25$ unit cells of a $5\\times5$ grid such that:\n\neach cell contains at most one chip\nall chips in the same row and all chips in the same column have the same colour\nany additional chip placed on the grid would violate one or more of the previous two conditions.\n\nWhen ready, output the final answer enclosed in <answer> and </answer> tags. Do not generate any content after the </answer> tag. When ready, output the final answer enclosed in <answer> and </answer> tags. Do not generate any content after the </answer> tag.\n- **Sub-Goal:** - To generate possible configurations for placing white and black chips on a 5×5 grid satisfying all given constraints using an automated method.\n\n4.\n- **Tool Name:** Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\n- **Tool Metadata:** {\'tool_name\': \'Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool\', \'tool_description\': \'A generalized tool that takes query from the user, and answers the question step by step to the best of its ability. It can also accept an image.\', \'tool_version\': \'1.0.0\', \'input_types\': {\'query\': \'str - The query that includes query from the user to guide the agent to generate response.\'}, \'output_type\': \'str - The generated response to the original query\', \'demo_commands\': [{\'command\': \'execution = tool.execute(query="Summarize the following text in a few lines")\', \'description\': \'Generate a short summary given the query from the user.\'}], \'user_metadata\': {\'limitation\': \'\\nThe Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool may provide hallucinated or incorrect responses.\\n\', \'best_practice\': "\\nFor optimal results with the Generalist_Solution_Generator_Tool:\\n1. Use it for general queries or tasks that don\'t require specialized knowledge or specific tools in the toolbox.\\n2. Provide clear, specific query.   \\n3. Use it to answer the original query through step by step reasoning for tasks without complex or multi-step reasoning.\\n4. For complex queries, break them down into subtasks and use the tool multiple times.\\n5. Use it as a starting point for complex tasks, then refine with specialized tools.\\n6. Verify important information from its responses.\\n"}, \'require_llm_engine\': True}\n- **Relevant Data:** - The task is to determine the number of ways to place indistinguishable white and black chips in a 5×5 grid while adhering to certain constraints (each cell contains at most one chip, all chips in each row and column must be the same color, no additional chip can be placed without violating these rules).\n\n3.\n\nInstructions:\n1.  Analyze the tool\'s required parameters from its metadata.\n2.  Construct valid Python code that addresses the sub-goal using the provided context and data.\n3.  The command must include at least one call to `tool.execute()`.\n4.  Each `tool.execute()` call must be assigned to a variable named **`execution`**.\n5.  Please give the exact numbers and parameters should be used in the `tool.execute()` call.\n\nOutput Format:\nPresent your response in the following structured format. Do not include any extra text or explanations.\n\nGenerated Command:\n```python\n<command>\n```\n\nExample1:\nGenerated Command:\n```python\nexecution = tool.execute(query="Summarize the following porblom:"Isaac has 100 toys, masa gets ...., how much are their together?")\n```\n\nExample2:\nGenerated Command:\n```python\nexecution = tool.execute(query=["Methanol", "function of hyperbola", "Fermat\'s Last Theorem"])\n```\n', 'gen_ai.response.id': 'a0c73c9d-da83-4510-85bd-fdcc270a72e5', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.openai.system_fingerprint': 'a26a7955944dc5c60445bff77fac9c8e', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 942, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 827, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 115, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': 'Generated Command:\n```python\nexecution = tool.execute(query="There is a collection of 25 indistinguishable white chips and 25 indistinguishable black chips. Find the number of ways to place some of these chips in the 25 unit cells of a 5x5 grid such that: each cell contains at most one chip, all chips in the same row and all chips in the same column have the same colour, and any additional chip placed on the grid would violate one or more of the previous two conditions. Please solve this step by step and provide the final answer.")\n```'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'openai.chat.completion', 'context': {'trace_id': '0x734333be6fd8df73000db50559ceb701', 'span_id': '0x3fb42cf42f0db68f', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.CLIENT', 'parent_id': None, 'start_time': '2026-08-25T08:31:28.750466Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T08:31:38.057611Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'OK'}, 'attributes': {'gen_ai.request.type': 'chat', 'gen_ai.system': 'OpenAI', 'gen_ai.request.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.request.max_tokens': 4000, 'gen_ai.request.temperature': 0, 'gen_ai.request.top_p': 0.99, 'gen_ai.request.streaming': False, 'gen_ai.prompt.0.role': 'system', 'gen_ai.prompt.0.content': 'You are a helpful assistant.', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.role': 'user', 'gen_ai.prompt.1.content': 'There is a collection of 25 indistinguishable white chips and 25 indistinguishable black chips. Find the number of ways to place some of these chips in the 25 unit cells of a 5x5 grid such that: each cell contains at most one chip, all chips in the same row and all chips in the same column have the same colour, and any additional chip placed on the grid would violate one or more of the previous two conditions. Please solve this step by step and provide the final answer.', 'gen_ai.response.id': 'd1bdf71b-b124-4d30-aabd-c6c1856e8382', 'gen_ai.response.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.openai.system_fingerprint': 'a26a7955944dc5c60445bff77fac9c8e', 'gen_ai.usage.total_tokens': 1334, 'gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens': 111, 'gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens': 1223, 'gen_ai.completion.0.finish_reason': 'stop', 'gen_ai.completion.0.role': 'assistant', 'gen_ai.completion.0.content': 'We have a 5×5 grid, and we place chips such that:\n\n1. Each cell has at most one chip.\n2. In each row, all chips are the same color.\n3. In each column, all chips are the same color.\n4. The arrangement is *maximal* — you cannot add another chip without breaking rule 2 or 3.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1 – Understanding the constraints\n\nIf in a row there is at least one chip, then *all* chips in that row must be the same color.  \nSimilarly, if in a column there is at least one chip, then *all* chips in that column must be the same color.\n\nThis means:  \n- If a row has a white chip, then every chip in that row is white.  \n- If a column has a white chip, then every chip in that column is white.\n\nSo the color of a cell is determined by the row color and column color.  \nIf a row is "white" and a column is "white", the intersection cell is white.  \nIf a row is "white" and a column is "black", the intersection cell cannot have a chip (because it would have to be both white and black).  \nSimilarly for other combinations.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2 – Structure of a valid configuration\n\nLet’s classify rows and columns by color:\n\n- Let \\( r_W \\) = number of rows that are "white" (meaning all chips in them are white).  \n- Let \\( r_B \\) = number of rows that are "black".  \n- Let \\( c_W \\) = number of columns that are "white".  \n- Let \\( c_B \\) = number of columns that are "black".\n\nA chip can only be placed at the intersection of a row and column of the *same* color.  \nSo:\n\n- White chips can only be in cells where row is white and column is white.  \n- Black chips can only be in cells where row is black and column is black.\n\nThus the grid is divided into four blocks:\n\n- \\( r_W \\times c_W \\) block: can contain white chips.  \n- \\( r_B \\times c_B \\) block: can contain black chips.  \n- The other two blocks (\\( r_W \\times c_B \\) and \\( r_B \\times c_W \\)) must be empty.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3 – Maximality condition\n\nThe arrangement is maximal: you cannot add any chip without violating the color rule.\n\nConsider an empty cell in the \\( r_W \\times c_B \\) block.  \nIf we put a white chip there, the row is white, but the column is black — that would violate the column rule.  \nIf we put a black chip there, the row is white — violates row rule.  \nSo those cells are *unfillable* regardless.\n\nSimilarly for \\( r_B \\times c_W \\) block.\n\nNow consider an empty cell in the \\( r_W \\times c_W \\) block.  \nIf it’s empty, we could put a white chip there without breaking rules (row is white, column is white).  \nSo for maximality, **every cell in the \\( r_W \\times c_W \\) block must be filled**.  \nSimilarly, every cell in the \\( r_B \\times c_B \\) block must be filled.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4 – Consequences\n\nSo the filled cells are exactly:\n\n- All \\( r_W \\times c_W \\) cells are white.  \n- All \\( r_B \\times c_B \\) cells are black.\n\nThe total number of chips is:\n\n\\[\nr_W c_W + r_B c_B\n\\]\n\nWe have 25 white chips and 25 black chips available, but we don’t have to use all.  \nHowever, maximality means we fill all possible cells in those blocks.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5 – Counting possibilities\n\nWe need to choose:\n\n- Which rows are white: \\( r_W \\) rows out of 5.  \n- Which columns are white: \\( c_W \\) columns out of 5.\n\nThen \\( r_B = 5 - r_W \\), \\( c_B = 5 - c_W \\).\n\nThe number of white chips used = \\( r_W c_W \\), must be ≤ 25 (always true since max is 25).  \nThe number of black chips used = \\( r_B c_B \\), must be ≤ 25 (also always true).\n\nSo any \\( r_W, c_W \\) from 0 to 5 works.\n\n---\n\n### Step 6 – Are all choices distinct?\n\nYes, because the choice of which rows are white and which columns are white completely determines the arrangement.\n\nNumber of ways:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{r_W=0}^{5} \\sum_{c_W=0}^{5} \\binom{5}{r_W} \\binom{5}{c_W}\n\\]\n\nThis is:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\sum_{r=0}^5 \\binom{5}{r} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{c=0}^5 \\binom{5}{c} \\right) = 2^5 \\cdot 2^5 = 32 \\cdot 32 = 1024\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 7 – Check edge cases\n\n- If \\( r_W = 0 \\), then no white rows, so no white chips; all rows are black, so all columns must be black for chips to exist. But if \\( c_W > 0 \\), then white columns exist but no white rows → no white chips, but black chips can only be in black rows/black columns. That’s fine.  \n- If \\( r_W = 5 \\), all rows white, then all columns must be white for chips; if \\( c_W < 5 \\), black columns exist but no black rows → no black chips. Still valid.\n\nAll 1024 configurations satisfy maximality.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1024}\n\\]'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'openai.chat.completion', 'context': {'trace_id': '0x967a34a19f45d67c900108fb5fe08bf8', 'span_id': '0x16ec153e5768017c', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.CLIENT', 'parent_id': '0x5dccca7cfa73cd16', 'start_time': '2026-08-25T08:31:38.060015Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T08:31:40.236705Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'OK'}, 'attributes': {'gen_ai.request.type': 'chat', 'gen_ai.system': 'OpenAI', 'gen_ai.request.model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'gen_ai.request.max_tokens': 4000, 'gen_ai.request.temperature': 0, 'gen_ai.request.top_p': 0.99, 'gen_ai.request.streaming': False, 'gen_ai.prompt.0.role': 'system', 'gen_ai.prompt.0.