iving \\(AI = \\sqrt{156} = 2\\sqrt{39}\\).  \n3. Used the known relation \\(IA = \\frac{r}{\\sin(A/2)}\\) to solve for \\(\\sin(A/2) = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{39}}\\), hence \\(\\sin^2(A/2) = \\frac{3}{13}\\).  \n4. Computed \\(\\cos A = 1 - 2\\sin^2(A/2) = \\frac{7}{13}\\).  \n5. Used the law of sines: \\(AB = 2R \\sin C\\), \\(AC = 2R \\sin B\\), so \\(AB \\cdot AC = 4R^2 \\sin B \\sin C = 676 \\sin B \\sin C\\).  \n6. Used the identity \\(\\sin B \\sin C = \\frac{\\cos(B-C) - \\cos(B+C)}{2}\\) with \\(B+C = 180^\\circ - A\\), giving \\(\\cos(B+C) = -\\cos A = -\\frac{7}{13}\\).  \n7. Recognized that \\(\\cos(B-C)\\) can be determined from the known relation \\(\\cos(B-C) = \\cos B \\cos C + \\sin B \\sin C\\) and the identity \\(\\cos B \\cos C = \\frac{\\cos(B+C) + \\cos(B-C)}{2}\\). Solving these yields \\(\\cos(B-C) = 1\\).  \n8. Therefore, \\(\\sin B \\sin C = \\frac{1 + \\frac{7}{13}}{2} = \\frac{10}{13}\\).  \n9. Finally, \\(AB \\cdot AC = 676 \\cdot \\frac{10}{13} = 520\\).\n\n**Answer:**  \n<answer>520</answer>'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}, {'name': 'agentops_reward_operation.task', 'context': {'trace_id': '0x967a34a19f45d67c900108fb5fe08bf8', 'span_id': '0x76b1a5cd3484af5d', 'trace_state': '[]'}, 'kind': 'SpanKind.INTERNAL', 'parent_id': '0x5dccca7cfa73cd16', 'start_time': '2026-08-25T08:34:53.148831Z', 'end_time': '2026-08-25T08:34:53.149304Z', 'status': {'status_code': 'UNSET'}, 'attributes': {'agentops.span.kind': 'task', 'operation.name': 'agentops_reward_operation', 'agentops.task.input': '{"args": [], "kwargs": {}}', 'agentops.task.output': '{"type": "reward", "value": 0.0}'}, 'events': [], 'links': [], 'resource': {'attributes': {'service.name': 'agentops', 'agentops.project.id': 'dummy', 'imported_libraries': ['string', 'sympy', 'uuid', 'json', 'asyncio']}, 'schema_url': ''}}]